===Etymology 4===
Of {{unc|non|nocap=1}} origin. De Vries considers the word to be derived from a earlier form related to {{cog|gem-pro|*hōhô|t=plow}},<ref name=AnEW /> while others take the word as possibly derived from {{der|non|gem-pro|*hawwaną|t=to hew, cut}}, and related to {{cog|frk|*hauwan}}. {{rfv-etym|non}}

====Noun====
{{non-noun|m}}

# {{senseid|non|dogfish}} [[spiny dogfish]]
#* {{Q|non|First Grammatical Treatise|84|22|quote=''Har'' vex á kykvendum, en '''''hȧr''''' er fiskr.|trans=''Hair'' grows on living things, but ''har'' is a fish.}}

=====Usage notes=====
The {{w|First Grammarian}} says that this word had a long nasalized vowel, marked with an overdot, and contrasts it with {{m|non|hár|t=hair|id=hair}}, which does not.

